# UST.G3CQ: Selected-Source Transform-Defect Correction Theorem

## Statement

At the selected `GF(11)`, `gamma=3`, `a=0` proof fiber, let the exact G3CC
terminal H02 source be divided by the fixed B69 Groebner basis after insertion
of the G3BI pole-six correction numerator.  Its 225 selected multipliers are
denoted by `LS_j`.  If `q'_j` are the exact G3CN quotient jets, then

```text
d_selected = sum_j q'_j LS_j
```

is an explicit nonzero polynomial of Cox degree `(9,1,3)` with 705 terms.
Complete Groebner division has zero residual and uses 107 generators, all of
which belong to the frozen 225-generator transform.

Consequently the frozen transform emits an exact ten-row coefficient vector
`c_selected` satisfying

```text
J(0) c_selected = d_selected.
```

With the G3CN sign convention

```text
g_j = J(a) T_j(a) + a q'_j + O(a^2),
```

the corrected source preimage is obtained by adding `+a c_selected`.  Its
first-return contribution is therefore

```text
R_correction = - sum_i partial_i(c_selected_i).
```

The ten coefficient rows contain 62,053 terms.  Their independently replayed
minus divergence has 11,222 ambient H02 terms and a 229-coordinate B103 H02
normal form.

## Meaning

The nonzero G3CN quotient jet is not a selected-source obstruction.  For this
physical source it is absorbed entirely by the already certified finite
transform; no larger pole-six support or raw `a=1` rank calculation is needed.
This theorem closes the quotient-defect correction and its first H02 return at
the selected proof fiber.

It does not yet claim a characteristic-zero family action, a complete
connection derivative, path integration, an integral period, or `beta_C`.
The exact recursive propagation of the emitted H02 row is UST.G3CR.

